  "summary": "BMEX is a distressed zombie microcap after BitMEX announced its permanent shutdown on July 23, 2026. Current market cap ~$228K (down from ~$6M a week ago), fixed circulating supply of 99.75M, so mcap tracks price. Strong post-crash downtrend but visibly decelerating (last 24h only -9.8% vs -30%+ earlier), with price near its all-time-low floor (~$0.0017). Over the 9-day horizon to Aug 6, a Monte Carlo with uncertain mildly-negative decaying drift and high daily vol (0.15-0.28, fat tails) yields median ~$175K, with wide bands reflecting continued-bleed risk (open lower bound allows sub-$100K, ~25% mass) and thin-volume speculative bounce potential. Upper tail exceeds $1.5M only ~1%.",
  "reasoning": "My forecast for the BMEX token market capitalization on August 6, 2026:\n\n**Median: ~$175,000** (P10: $57K, P90: $538K)\n\n**Key reasoning:**\n- BMEX is a distressed zombie microcap following BitMEX's July 23 shutdown announcement. Current market cap is ~$228K (down from ~$6M a week prior), with fixed circulating supply of 99.75M tokens, so market cap tracks price directly.\n- The post-crash decline is strong but visibly decelerating (last 24h only -9.8% vs -30%+ drops on earlier days), with the price hovering near its all-time-low floor of ~$0.0017.\n- Over the 9-day horizon, a Monte Carlo simulation using post-crash returns (excluding the -91% crash day), a mildly-negative decaying drift, and high daily volatility (0.15-0.28 with fat tails) produced the distribution.\n- The open lower bound captures meaningful continued-bleed risk (~25% probability below $100K), while thin trading volume ($4K/day) leaves room for speculative pump spikes in the upper tail. Exceeding $1.5M is only ~1% likely.",
